# SnapSurf Intel x86_64 Pipeline Notes

Scope: root ASM/NASM foundation only. These notes constrain compiler/runtime
work; they are not executed by `make`.

Target baseline:
- Linux x86_64 ELF64.
- System V AMD64 ABI for user function calls.
- Integer foundation path uses GPRs first: `rax` return value, `rdi/rsi/rdx/rcx/r8/r9`
  for the first six integer arguments.

Current generated-call contract:
- `_start` calls `main`.
- Every SnapSurf function emits:
  - `push rbp`
  - `mov rbp, rsp`
  - optional `sub rsp, rounded_stack_bytes`
  - parameter register spills to `[rbp - slot]`
  - body
  - return epilogue from `ret expr`
- Stack reservation is rounded to 16 bytes so nested `call` instructions do not
  inherit odd local-slot alignment.

Do not weaken:
- Do not call C/Rust runtime helpers from the root foundation path.
- Do not hide function-call lowering behind a runtime dispatcher.
- Do not emit a label name that cannot be resolved from semantic registry data.
